<section class="section tight"><div class="wrap prose">
  <h2>1. Discovery</h2><p>The assistant asks about your business, goals, budget and timeline. It recommends the smallest set of services that solves your need and shows prices from our live catalog. If something needs custom work, you get a quote request, never a made-up number.</p>
  <h2>2. Proposal &amp; checkout</h2><p>You can buy catalog services right away, or accept a written proposal that lists scope, deliverables, timeline, exclusions and an expiry date. Payment runs through Stripe Checkout, or you can request an invoice.</p>
  <h2>3. Onboarding</h2><p>Once you've paid, we open a project for each service and send you a short requirements form. Your portal shows every milestone.</p>
  <h2>4. Delivery by specialist agents</h2><p>A project-manager agent plans the work and assigns specialists: registration, website, application, brand, content and SEO. Each one drafts its part. A <b>separate QA agent</b> checks the work against your requirements and sends anything defective back.</p>
  <h2>5. Government filings</h2><p>For registrations and corporate filings you complete a guided form; submitting it authorizes us to file it for you. Our Filing Agent checks it against the registry's rules and submits it: automatically where the registry offers a filing API (such as BC Registries), through the official registry portal everywhere else. Work starts as soon as your order is paid, and nothing is filed that fails our checks.</p><h2>Human approval</h2><p>Domain transfers, DNS changes, website launches and refunds wait in our owner's approval queue.</p>
  <h2>6. Delivery, revisions &amp; support</h2><p>You review the deliverables, ask for changes or approve them. Support is available in your portal any time, and you can always ask for a person.</p>
  <h2>What the AI can't do</h2><ul><li>Invent prices, discounts or guarantees</li><li>Give legal, tax or accounting advice (it gives general information and tells you when to see a professional)</li><li>Move money, issue refunds or change payment details</li><li>Submit a government filing you didn't authorize, or publish/deploy without human approval</li><li>Share one customer's information with another</li></ul>
